This file records details of all data files in the data_input folder.

Format: file name - source - date added - description. "Used in" lists the scripts that read each file.

wind_solar_biodiversity_sysreview_v8_20260602.csv - Ruby Stephens and Malan Bothma - added 2024-12 - updated 2026-06-02 - main systematic map dataset. Bibliographic details of each included study (exported from Rayyan) plus data extracted manually from each study by Ruby Stephens and Malan Bothma. One row per study location (a study with several locations has several rows, numbered by location_no). Extracted fields include energy type (wind_solar), topic (impact_mitigation), development phase, study location (country, region, latitude/longitude and how they were obtained), habitat, biodiversity category, subcategory and metric, study taxa, study design, direction of effect for wind and solar, and suggested and tested mitigation (see Table S2 of the paper for categories). Used in: sysreview_analysis.R, supplementary_analyses/compare_gpkg_gipt.R, supplementary_analyses/preconstruction_gipt_analysis.R.

Rayyan_take3_export_articles.csv - Ruby Stephens - 2024-11-12 - Exported articles with labels and tags from third round of article screening for systematic review in Rayyan (https://www.rayyan.ai/). Used in: sysreview_dataprep.R, which splits the screening notes into columns (data_output/rayyan_export_processed.csv) as the starting point for the manual data extraction above. Does not need to be re-run.

Global-Wind-Power-Tracker-February-2025.xlsx and Global-Solar-Power-Tracker-February-2025.xlsx - Global Energy Monitor - added 2025-08-22 - Global Wind Power Tracker and Global Solar Power Tracker, February 2025 releases: locations, capacity, status and start year of utility-scale wind and solar power facilities worldwide. CC BY 4.0. Cite as Global Energy Monitor, Global Wind Power Tracker, February 2025 release, and Global Energy Monitor and TransitionZero, Global Solar Power Tracker, February 2025 release. https://globalenergymonitor.org/projects/global-wind-power-tracker/ and https://globalenergymonitor.org/projects/global-solar-power-tracker/. Used in: gipt_data.R (global facility locations compared with study locations, Table 1, Figure 1), supplementary_analyses/preconstruction_gipt_analysis.R.

Global-Wind-Power-Tracker-June-2024.xlsx and Global-Solar-Power-Tracker-June-2024-v2.xlsx - Global Energy Monitor - added 2025-01-22 - Global Wind Power Tracker and Global Solar Power Tracker, June 2024 releases. CC BY 4.0. Cite as Global Energy Monitor, Global Wind Power Tracker, June 2024 release, and Global Energy Monitor and TransitionZero, Global Solar Power Tracker, June 2024 release. Used in: spatial_dataprep.R (starting list of Australian facilities, which was then checked manually, see windsolar_gipt_aus_checked.csv), supplementary_analyses/compare_windsolar_datasources.R.

windsolar_gipt_aus_checked.csv - Ruby Stephens - updated 2025-02-24 - data on locations, capacity and start year of wind and solar facilities located across Australia. Original list from the Global Energy Monitor June 2024 trackers (data_output/windsolar_gipt_aus.csv) manually checked and updated using project websites and Google Earth. Only onshore projects operating or under construction and above 3MW capacity included. Used in: spatial_dataprep.R.

ibra7_biomes_background.shp (plus .cpg, .dbf, .prj, .shx) - Ruby Stephens - created 2021-03-05 - updated 2021-03-22 - Interim Biogeographic Regionalisation for Australia (IBRA) version 7 regions, each assigned to a biome from Olson et al. (2001) and Dinerstein et al. (2017), dissolved to biomes and simplified so that R displays it more easily. Used in: spatial_dataprep.R (biome of each facility), spatial_figures.R (Figure 5a).

mvg_codes_names.csv - Ruby Stephens - National Vegetation Information System (NVIS) Major Vegetation Group (MVG) codes (mvg_code) and names (mvg_name), with the simplified groups used in the paper (mvg_simplified; Table S4). Used in: spatial_dataprep.R to name the present-day and pre-1750 NVIS rasters in data_cache.

solar_nationalmap_20241203.csv and wind_nationalmap_20241203.csv - National Map - Ruby Stephens - 2024-12-03 - data downloaded from nationalmap.gov.au on locations and power generation of wind and solar facilities in the National Electricity Market (southeast Australia). Used only in supplementary_analyses/compare_windsolar_datasources.R, to check the Global Energy Monitor data against government data.
